<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Birka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 750–975</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Birka was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> trading town on the island of Björkö in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-malaren">Lake Mälaren</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, flourishing from the mid 8th to the late 10th century. Its merchants traded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">furs</a> and slaves for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and goods from the Frankish, Byzantine and Abbasid worlds, and the missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ansgar">Ansgar</a> preached there around 830. With nearby Hovgården it is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/birka.jpg" alt="Birka" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Holger.Ellgaard · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Birka_Ansgar_2008.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
